hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1386","Narrated Rafi' bin Khadij:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from a matter that was of benefit for us. When one of us had some land and we would let someone use it for a portion of its produce or some Dirham. He said: 'When one of you has some land then let him grant it to his brother"""""
"1387","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not prohibit share-cropping. But he ordered that they be helpful with each other"""""
"1388","Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged for the accidental blood-Money: Twenty Bint Makhad"""""
"1389","Narrator: Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them)\n\nIt was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr — that Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — from Ibn ʿAwn — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said:\n\nʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired a piece of land in Khaybar and said: \O Messenger of Allah"
"1390","Narrated 'Ikrimah:from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet (ﷺ) made the blood-money twelve thousand"
"1391","(Another chain) from 'Ikrimah from the Prophet (ﷺ) and it is similar but he did not mention \from Ibn 'Abbas\"" in it. There is much more criticism than this for (this) narration of Ibn 'Uyainah"""""
"1392","Narrated to us is the following: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us, Ayyūb reported to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father (ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr), from Saʿīd ibn Zayd (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n> \Whoever revives a dead (barren) land"
"1393","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood-money for the fingers on the hands and (the toes of) the feet is the same: Ten camels for each finger"""""
"1394","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \These and these are the same.\"" referring to the little finger and thumb"""""
"1395","Narrated Abu As-Safar:\A man from the Quraish broke a tooth of a man from the Ansar. So he appealed to Mu'awiyah against him. He said to Mu'awiyah: 'O Commander of the Believers! This person broke one of my teeth.' Mu'awiyah said: 'We will try to get satisfaction for you.' And the other person insisted that Mu'awiyah get him to agree [but he was not satisfied]. So Mu'awiyah said him: 'It is up to your companion.' Abu Ad-Darda' was sitting with him"""""
"1396","Narrated Anas:that a girl went out in Al-Madinah wearing some silver ornaments. A Jew grabbed her and fractured her head with a stone"
"1397","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed the first cases to be judged between the people are those of bloodshed"""""
"1398","Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\Indeed the first cases to be judged between the worshippers are those of bloodshed"""""
"1399","Narrated Abul-Hakam Al-Bajali:\I heard Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah mentioning from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: 'If the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth all took part in shedding the blood of believer"""""
"1400","Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The father does not suffer retaliation for [killing] the son"""""
"1401","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'The Hudud are not carried in the Masjid"
"1402","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The blood of a Muslim man"""""
"1403","Sa‘īd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us, from ‘Amr ibn Dīnār, from ‘Ikrimah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it, and he did not mention in it [a chain going back to] Ibn ‘Abbās. In the ḥadīth of Ibn ‘Uyaynah there is more wording than this. Abū ‘Īsā said: \We do not know of anyone who mentions in this ḥadīth [a chain going back to] Ibn ‘Abbās other than Muḥammad ibn Muslim.\"" The practice according to this ḥadīth is held by some of the scholars"
"1404","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Prophet (ﷺ) assigned the same blood-money for the two 'Amiris as that of the Muslims"""""
"1405","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\When Allah granted His Messenger (ﷺ) victory over Makkah"""""
"1406","Narrated Abu Shuraih Al-Ka'bi:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah made Makkah sacred"""""
"1407","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\A man was killed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"""""
"1408","Narrated Buraidah:from his father who said: \Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched a commander of an army he would exhort him personally; that he should have Taqwa of Allah"""""
"1409","Narrated Shaddad bin Aws:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed Allah has decreed Ihsan in everything. So when you kill"""""
"1410","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that a Ghurrah male slave or female slave be given in the case of a fetus. The one of the judgement was made against said: 'Should we give something for one who did not drink"""""
"1411","Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān, narrated by Wahb ibn Jarīr, narrated by Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"
"1412","Abu Juhaifah said:\I said to 'Ali: O Commander of the Believers! Do you have anything written that is not in Allah's Book?' He said: 'By the One Who splits the seed and creates the soul"""""
"1413","Al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from Yazīd al-Raqāshī, Abū al-Ḥakam al-Bajalī narrated to us, he said: I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah — may Allāh be pleased with them both — mentioning that the Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:\n\n\Were the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth to conspire together upon the blood of a single believer"
"1414","Narrated Samurah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever kills his slave"""""
"1415","Narrated Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab:that 'Umar would say: \The blood-money upon the tribe"""""
"1416","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:\A man bit the hand of another man. The man who was bitten pulled his hand out"""""
"1417","Hannād narrated to us, Abū Mu‘āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A‘mash, from ‘Abdullāh ibn Murrah, from Masrūq, from ‘Abdullāh ibn Mas‘ūd رضي الله عنه, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n“The blood of a Muslim who testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful to shed except in one of three cases: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who forsakes his religion and separates from the community.”\n\nHe (the narrator) said: “In this chapter there are narrations from ‘Uthmān, ‘Ā’ishah, and Ibn ‘Abbās رضي الله"
"1418","Narrated Sa'eed bin Zaid bin 'Amr bin Nufail:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is killed over his wealth then he is a martyr. [And whoever steals a hand-span of land"""""
"1419","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is killed over his wealth"""""
"1420","Narrated by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When Allah granted victory to His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) over Makkah"
"1421","and he fights and is killed, then he is a martyr. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1420 Arabic Hadees: 1420\"" 1422"""""
"1422","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man was killed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so the killer was handed over to the victim's heir. The killer said: ""O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not intend to kill him."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Indeed, if he was truthful and you killed him, you would enter the Fire."" So the man let him go. He (Abu Hurayrah) said: And he was bound with a rope (nisa'ah). He said: So he went out dragging his rope. He said: So he came to be known as Dhu al-Nisa'ah (the man with the rope). Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. And the nisa'ah is a rope."
